{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0H3I", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e042a87b2a675c01d8506d66630146b2639495b97a5c82cbf6b7aff2eb634038", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is the obligatory lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:99d1a0dd498ee2a8b0a2f67d661ab75d45f401d0f5a9388b211f467773344032", "unit_id": "tag:0H3I:prose-0006"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0H3I", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "MATH_0007": "$X = \\bigcup X_j$", "MATH_0008": "$X_j$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-affine-weakly-normal}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-affine-weakly-normal}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-weakly-normal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:555b2b125c46a99a2b385a173afe2abdca090cb0d8ed322725f9e75886cb4b24", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fb3625676da4cb85a46ae2a0a8793f613cf332836c6263c035ff79b3b723ba37", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme such that every quasi-compact open has\nfinitely many irreducible components. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The scheme <MATH_0002> is weakly normal.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every affine open <MATH_0003> the ring <MATH_0004>\nsatisfies conditions (1) and (2) of Lemma <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0005> such that\neach ring <MATH_0006>\nsatisfies conditions (1) and (2) of Lemma <REF_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0005> There exists an open covering <MATH_0007>\nsuch that each open subscheme <MATH_0008> is weakly normal.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0009> is weakly normal then every open subscheme is weakly normal.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bb25e853d031aba65cf11de38905dec47933451bc0021ef3d34d1058f9843829", "unit_id": "tag:0H3U:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0H3I", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X^{wn} = X^{X^\\nu/wn} \\to X$", "MATH_0003": "$X^\\nu \\to X$", "MATH_0004": "$X^{X^\\nu/wn}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-relative-seminormalization}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5899122086d5f739c1f31b524058bb219087d2ab27aaeca064e48bbc190eb17e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f7055670f9302addc3bbdfbf126936ac60a7a451b60eb64b55a80140c3259b0a", "source_text": "The condition to <MATH_0001> be weakly normal is that the morphism\n<MATH_0002> is an isomorphism. Since the construction\nof <MATH_0003> commutes with base change to open subschemes\nand since the construction of <MATH_0004> commutes with base\nchange to open subschemes of <MATH_0005> (Lemma <REF_0001>)\nthe lemma is clear.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:13e8a57131595a46a19f2e19f78a74dc26c881dc5e7dc4979bc2de6649d5e554", "unit_id": "tag:0H3U:proof"}
